https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/blob/33272a04994e81509fbd713c8dc1217c39f1e461/proxy/proxy.go#L599-L602

Domain-based routing rules were ignored for WireGuard connections due to two issues: (1) PR #4030 commented out critical lines that set inbound and content tags before dispatch, and (2) concurrent `Process()` calls from multiple peers could overwrite shared routing info.

## Changes

- Added `sync.RWMutex` to protect `Server.info` field from concurrent access
- `Process()`: write-locks when updating routing info  
- `forwardConnection()`: read-locks and copies routing info locally before use
- **Restored inbound and content tag setting** right before `Dispatch()` call (commented out in PR #4030)

## Technical Details

The WireGuard server stores routing configuration (dispatcher, context, sniffing settings) in `Server.info`. Two problems prevented proper routing:

1. **Missing context tags**: PR #4030 commented out lines that set `inboundTag` and `contentTag` in the context right before dispatch, breaking domain-based routing
2. **Race conditions**: Multiple concurrent peer connections could overwrite `s.info`, causing inconsistent routing configuration

```go
// Before: unsafe concurrent access and missing tag setting
func (s *Server) forwardConnection(dest net.Destination, conn net.Conn) {
    if s.info.dispatcher == nil { // race: s.info may be overwritten here
        return
    }
    ctx := core.ToBackgroundDetachedContext(s.info.ctx) // race
    // ... missing inbound/content tag setting before dispatch
    link, err := s.info.dispatcher.Dispatch(ctx, dest)
}

// After: thread-safe access with restored tag setting
func (s *Server) forwardConnection(dest net.Destination, conn net.Conn) {
    s.infoMu.RLock()
    info := s.info  // atomic snapshot
    s.infoMu.RUnlock()

    if info.dispatcher == nil {
        return
    }
    // ... prepare context

    // Restore tag setting (was commented out in PR #4030)
    if info.inboundTag != nil {
        ctx = session.ContextWithInbound(ctx, info.inboundTag)
    }
    if info.contentTag != nil {
        ctx = session.ContextWithContent(ctx, info.contentTag)
    }

    link, err := info.dispatcher.Dispatch(ctx, dest)
}
```

This fix addresses the regression introduced in PR #4030 while also protecting against race conditions in multi-peer deployments.

