My use case for it is this: I have a private internal web server that can only be accessed via xray. I have it configured like this:
```
{
      "tag": "privateserver",
      "protocol": "freedom",
      "settings": {
        "redirect": "127.0.0.1:38462",
        "finalRules": [
          {
            "ip": [
              "127.0.0.1"
            ],
            "port": "38462",
            "action": "allow",
            "network": "tcp"
          }
        ],
        "proxyProtocol": 2
      }
    }
```

The server needs to see the IP of the client, which is why I have proxy protocol configured. However, if the client connects to xray using UDP based protocol such as hysteria2, the proxy protocol fails to pass the correct client ip to the web server and instead passes 127.0.0.1. 

Do you have any suggestions on how the web server can reliably get the client ip?

